---
description: Do not write thinking-out-loud or process commentary in PM reports.
alwaysApply: true
---

# No thinking out loud

PMs want the finding, not a tour of how the document is organized or how you chose to write it.

Do not explain the report to the reader. Do not narrate methods policy, tone, or section purpose.

Forbidden patterns:

- "This appendix is the only place we name methods."
- "The body of the report stays in plain English."
- "As mentioned above", "we will now", "in this section we", "before we dive in".
- Staging the analysis ("first we look at X, then we consider Y").

```markdown
# ❌ BAD
This appendix is the only place we name methods. The body of the report stays in plain English.

**Funnel rates.** A funnel is a headcount at each step...

# ✅ GOOD
**Funnel rates.** A funnel is a headcount at each step...
```

Start the appendix with the first concept. If a sentence is about the writing, cut it.
